{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And she went into the field, etc.</b> Rashi explained: He showed him the signs of the patriarchs, and needs explanation according to its meaning. This is what it says: at first she stood in the field opposite him, where there is room to turn right and left — a hint to him that if he wishes to curse the seed of Abraham, he may curse to the right and to the left: the children of Ishmael on one side and the children of Keturah on the other side, but 'do not go in the middle' — do not curse the seed of Isaac. And afterward she stood in a path of the vineyards, where there is no room except to go two men abreast, and a hint to him that if he comes to curse the seed of Isaac, he can only curse from one side, which is from the side of Esau, but not from the other side, from the side of Jacob. And afterward she stood in a narrow place where there is no room to turn right and left, for all his children are fit, which is the seed of Jacob. This is 'the signs of the patriarchs' that He showed him."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The feminine subject (תאמר/ותלך) is the she-ass; 'he' and 'him' throughout refer to Balaam. The phrase צריך פי' לפי' is rendered as 'needs explanation according to its meaning.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:59.600028283Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}